ref="/primefaces-interview-questions">PrimeFaces Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/richfaces-interview-questions">RichFaces Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/gwt-interview-questions">Top 20+ GWT Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/jdb-interview-questions">Top 20 JDB Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/jogl-interview-questions">Top 15 JOGL Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/jbpm-interview-questions">Top 20 jBPM Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/jenkins-interview-questions">Jenkins Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/java-constructor-interview-questions">Java Constructor Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/java-technical-architect-interview-questions">Technical Architect Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/array-interview-questions-in-java">Array Interview Questions in Java for Freshers (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/java-generics-questions">Java Generics Questions</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item" style="background-color:var(--sidebar)"><h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading7"><button aria-controls="flush-collapse7" aria-expanded="true" class="accordion-button sidebar-btn" data-bs-target="#flush-collapse7" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">Database Interview</button></h2><div aria-labelledby="flush-heading7" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" id="flush-collapse7"><div class="accordion-body"><ul><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/dbms-interview-questions">Top 60+ DBMS Interview Questions and Answers (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/sql-interview-questions">SQL Interview Questions</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/pl-sql-interview-questions">PL/SQL Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-interview-questions">Oracle Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/mysql-interview-questions">Top 90+ MySQL Interview Questions and Answers (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/sql-server-interview-questions">SQL Server Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/mongodb-interview-questions">Top 50 MongoDB Interview Questions and Answers (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/cassandra-interview-questions-and-answers">Cassandra Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/db2-interview-questions-and-answers">DB2 Interview Questions and Answers</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/microsoft-access-interview-questions-and-answers">Microsoft Access Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/sqlite-interview-questions">SQLite Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/couchdb-interview-questions">CouchDB Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/neo4j-interview-questions-and-answers">Neo4j Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/mariadb-interview-questions">Top 30+ MariaDB Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/pouchdb-interview-questions">PouchDB Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/redis-interview-questions-and-answers">Redis Interview Questions (2025)</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/50-statistics-interview-questions-and-answers-for-data-scientists-for-2025">50+ Statistics Interview Questions and Answers for Data Scientists for 2025</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-12 col-md-7"><div class="overview"><div id="city"><table><tbody><tr><td><h1 class="h1">Microsoft Recruitment Process</h1><div style="font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:#6f6e6e"><span>17 Mar 2025</span> | <span><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 25 min read</span></div><h2 class="h2">Company Overview</h2><p>Microsoft is a multinational PC innovation enterprise headquartered in Redmond, Washington. It creates licenses backings and offers PC programming, shopper gadgets, PCs, and do administrations. Its best-known programming items are the Microsoft Windows line of working frameworks, the Microsoft Office suite, and the Internet Explorer and Edge internet browsers.</p><p>Microsoft also provides programming for work areas and servers, including Internet look (with Bing), the advanced administrations showcase (through MSN), blended reality (HoloLens), distributed computing (Azure) and programming improvement (Visual Studio).</p><p>Microsoft was established by Paul Allen and Bill Gates on April 4, 1975, and rose to overwhelm the PC working framework showcase with MS-DOS in the mid-1980s, trailed by Microsoft Windows. Since 1990, the organization made various corporate acquisitions. Their biggest acquisition was securing of LinkedIn for $26.2 billion in December 2016, trailed by their procurement of Skype Technologies for $8.5 billion in May 2011.</p><h2 class="h2">Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>Candidates must have 60% throughout in academics (class X, XI, Graduation, and Post-Graduation).</p><p>No education gap of more than one year.</p><p>Candidate should have good knowledge of C, C++, JAVA, DBMS, and Networking etc.</p><h2 class="h2">Selection Process</h2><p>The selection process of the company consists of 3 rounds. These rounds are as follows:</p><p>The Pattern of Written Exams:</p><table class="alt"><tbody><tr><th>Sections</th><th>No. Of Questions</th></tr><tr><td>Aptitude</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>English</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Technical</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>40</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The total time given to the questions is 1 hour 40 minutes. There is no negative marking in the exam.</p><h2 class="h2">Round 1</h2><p>The first round consists of 100 Multiple Choice Question. There is no negative marking. This test would cover the following topics:</p><h3 class="h3">Quantitative Ability</h3><ul class="points"><li>Number System</li><li>HCF &amp; LCM</li><li>Average</li><li>Profit &amp; Loss</li><li>Percentage</li><li>Time, Speed &amp; Distance</li><li>Logarithm</li><li>Odd Man Out &amp; Series</li><li>Probability</li><li>Permutation &amp; Combination</li><li>Boats &amp; Streams</li><li>Alligation or Mixtures</li><li>Simple Interest</li><li>Compound Interest</li></ul><h3 class="h3">English</h3><ul class="points"><li>Spotting Errors</li><li>One Word Substitution</li><li>Ordering of Sentences</li><li>Ordering of Words</li><li>Completing Statement</li><li>Sentence Correction</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Round 2</h2><p>Technical Ability: This is a technical ability round. In this round, they asked the technical questions from C, C++, JAVA, Networking, Operating System, and DBMS.</p><h2 class="h2">Round 3</h2><p>The third round is HR interview. Students who clear the technical round will be eligible for this round.</p><p><strong>You may expect HR round like:</strong></p><ol class="points"><li>Tell us about yourself.</li><li>Why should we hire you?</li><li>Do you consider yourself successful?</li><li>Are you willing to travel?</li><li>What is your greatest strengths &amp; weakness?</li><li>Tell me about your dream job.</li><li>Why did you leave your last job?</li><li>Are you a team player?</li><li>How do you feel about working nights and weekends?</li><li>Can you work under pressure?</li></ol><hr/><h2 class="h2 center">Microsoft Aptitude Questions</h2><hr/><h2 class="h4">1) A number when divided consecutively by 4 and 5 leaves remainder 1 and 4 respectively. When it is continuously divided by 5 and 4, then the respective remainder will be</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>1, 2</li><li>2, 3</li><li>4, 2</li><li>None of these.</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(1)"><span id="btntext1">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer1"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">2) 8796 * 223 + 8796 * 77=?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>2638800</li><li>2538800</li><li>2436400</li><li>22356600</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(2)"><span id="btntext2">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer2"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>8796 * 223 + 8796 *77= 8796 * (223+77)<br>300=2638800</br></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">3) 3+ 33+ 333+3.33=?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>352.3</li><li>362.33</li><li>372.33</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(3)"><span id="btntext3">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer3"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q3.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">4) In how many distinct ways can the letters of the word 'OPTICAL' be classified so that the vowels constantly come together?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>420</li><li>620</li><li>720</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(4)"><span id="btntext4">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer4"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>The word 'OPTICAL' comprises 7 different letters.<br>When the vowels OIA are constantly together, they can be likely to form one letter.<br>Then, we have to sort the letters PTCL (OIA).<br/>Now, 5 letters can be sorted in 5! = 120 ways.<br/>The vowels (OIA) can be sorted among themselves in 3! = 6 ways.<br/>Required representation of ways = (120 x 6) = 720.</br></br></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">5) In how many ways can a bundle of 5 men and 2 women be made out of a sum of 7 men and 3 women?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>63</li><li>80</li><li>45</li><li>135</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(5)"><span id="btntext5">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer5"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q5.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">6) A can do a secure job in 12 days. B is 60% more efficient than A. How long does B alone take to do the same activity?</h2><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q6.png"/></p><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(6)"><span id="btntext6">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer6"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>The Ratio of time taken by A and B=160:100=8:5<br/>Suppose B alone takes days to do the job.<br/>Then 8: 5: 12: x= 8x = (5 x 12) = <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q6_1.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"> days.</img></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">7) A and B can do a task in 8 days, B and C can do the same task in 12 days. A, B and C together can complete it in 6 days. A and C together will do it in?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>6 days</li><li>8 days</li><li>10 days</li><li>12 days</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(7)"><span id="btntext7">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer7"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q7.png"/></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q7_1.png"/></p><p>So, A and C together will do the work in 8 days.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">8) One pipe can fill a tank three times as quickly as another pipe. If together the two funnels can fill the tank in 36 minutes, at that point the slower pipe alone will have the capacity to fill the tank :</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>81 min.</li><li>108 min.</li><li>144 min.</li><li>192 min</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(8)"><span id="btntext8">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer8"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the easy pipe alone fill the tank in x minutes.<br/>At that point, quicker pipe will fill it in x/3 minutes.</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q8.png"/></p><p>X=144 min.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">9) A substantial tanker can be filled by two pipes A and B in 60 minutes and 40 minutes exclusively. How long will it take to fill the tanker from the empty state if B is utilized for a fraction of the time and A and B fill it together for the other half?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>15 min</li><li>20 min</li><li>27.5 min</li><li>30 min</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(9)"><span id="btntext9">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer9"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> D</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q9.png"/></p><p>Assume the tank is filled in x minutes.</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q9_2.png"/></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q9_3.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">10) A tap can fill a container in 6 hours. After a large portion of the tank is filled, three more comparative taps are opened. What is the aggregate time taken to fill the container totally?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>3 hrs 15 min</li><li>3 hrs 45 min</li><li>4 hrs</li><li>4 hrs 15 min</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(10)"><span id="btntext10">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer10"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">11) When the price of a product was decreased by 10%, then the number sold increased by 30%. What was the effect on total revenue?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>17%</li><li>13%</li><li>14%</li><li>19%</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(11)"><span id="btntext11">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer11"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the price of product Rs.100 and let the original sale Rs.100 pieces</p><p>Then total revenue =Rs. (100x100) =Rs.10000</p><p>New revenue=Rs. (90x130) =Rs.11700</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q11.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">12) 8, 24, 12, 36, 18, 54, (....)</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>27</li><li>108</li><li>72</li><li>82</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(12)"><span id="btntext12">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer12"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Integers are multiplied by 3 and divided by 2</p><p>So, the next integer is 54/2=27</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">13) 4, -8, 16, -32, 64, (....)</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>128</li><li>-128</li><li>192</li><li>-192</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(13)"><span id="btntext13">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer13"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Each number is the measure number multiplied by 2</p><p>So the required integer is -128</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">14) A 30% Loss on Cost Price is what percentage loss on Selling Price?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>25%</li><li>30%</li><li>40%</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(14)"><span id="btntext14">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer14"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> D</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let CP=100, SP=70</p><p>Loss= 30/70*100=42.85%</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">15) What would be Compound Interest increased on the sum of Rs 9000/- at the rate of 11 p.c. p .a in 2 years?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs 2048.99</li><li>Rs 2088.90</li><li>Rs 2099.90</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(15)"><span id="btntext15">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer15"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">16) Find the ratio in which rice at Rs. 7.20 a kg is merged with rice at Rs. 5.70 a kg to produce a compound worth Rs. 6.30 a kg.</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>1:2</li><li>3:2</li><li>2:3</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(16)"><span id="btntext16">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer16"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">17) A man can queue at 5 km ph in still water. If the acceleration of the current is 1 km ph and it takes him 1 hour to queue to a place and come back, how long is the place?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>2.4 km</li><li>2.5 km</li><li>3 km</li><li>None</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(17)"><span id="btntext17">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer17"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Speed downstream = (5 + 1) km ph = 6 km ph.</p><p>Speed upstream = (5 - 1) km ph = 4 km ph.</p><p>Let the distance be x km</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q17.png"/></p><p>2x + 3x = 12</p><p>5x = 12</p><p>X= 2.4 km</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">18) A and B put loan into a business in the proportion 3 : 2. In the event that 5% of the aggregate value goes to charity and A share is Rs. 855, the aggregate value is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs1425</li><li>Rs.1500</li><li>Rs.1537.50</li><li>Rs.1576</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(18)"><span id="btntext18">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer18"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the total value be Rs. 100.</p><p>After paying to fund, A's contribution = Rs 95 x <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q18.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"> = Rs 57</img></p><p>If A's offer is Rs. 57, total profit = Rs. 100.</p><p>If A's offer Rs. 855, total profit = <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q18_1.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"> x 855=Rs 1500</img></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">19) A, B and C together idea of pleasing in themselves in a business adventure. It concurred that A would contribute Rs. 6500 for a half year, B, Rs. 8400 for 5 months and C, Rs. 10,000 for 3 months. A demand to be the dynamic part for which; he was to get 5% of the interest. The value earned was Rs. 7400. Figure the share of B in the value.</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs 1900</li><li>Rs 2660</li><li>Rs 2200</li><li>Rs 2400</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(19)"><span id="btntext19">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer19"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>For dealing with, A receive = 5% of Rs. 7400 = Rs. 370.</p><p>Balance = Rs. (7400 - 370) = Rs. 7030.</p><p>Ratio of their contribution = (6500 x 6) : (8400 x 5) : (10000 x 3)</p><p>= 39000 : 42000 : 30000</p><p>= 13 : 14 : 10</p><p>B's share = Rs.7030 X <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q19.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"> = 2660</img></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">20) Three partners shared the profit in a business in the proportion 5: 7: 8. They had joined forces for 14 months, 8 months and 7 months individually. What was the proportion of their investment?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>5: 7:8</li><li>20:49:64</li><li>30:20:21</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(20)"><span id="btntext20">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer20"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">21) The income A, B, C is in the proportion 2: 3: 5. In the event that the additions of 15%, 10%, and 20% are permitted separately in their pay rates, at that point what will be a new proportion of their income?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>3: 3:10</li><li>10:11:20</li><li>23:33:60</li><li>Cannot be determined</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(21)"><span id="btntext21">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer21"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q21.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">22) If 40% of a number is equivalent to two-third of another number, what is the proportion of first number to the second number?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>2 : 5</li><li>3 : 7</li><li>5 : 3</li><li>7 : 3</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(22)"><span id="btntext22">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer22"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q22.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">23) Two number are in the proportion 3:5. If 9 is subtracted from each, the new numbers are in the proportion 12: 23. The least number is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>27</li><li>33</li><li>49</li><li>55</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(23)"><span id="btntext23">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer23"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the numeral be 3x and 5x</p><p>Then, <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q23.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"/></p><p>23(3x - 9) = 12(5x - 9)</p><p>9x = 99</p><p>x = 11.</p><p>The least number = (3 x 11) = 33.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">24) In a pack, there are coins of 25 p, 10 p and 5 p in the proportion of 1: 2: 3. If there is Rs. 30 taking all things together, what number of 5 p coins is there?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>50</li><li>100</li><li>150</li><li>200</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(24)"><span id="btntext24">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer24"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the numeral of 25 p, 10 p, and 5 p coins be x, 2x, 3x separately.</p><p>Then, Total of their values = Rs <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q24.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"/></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q24_1.png"/></p><p>Subsequently, the quantity of 5 p coins = (3 x 50) = 150.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">25) A total of money at simple interest adds up to Rs. 815 out of 3 years and to Rs. 854 of every 4 years. The aggregate is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 650</li><li>Rs. 690</li><li>Rs. 698</li><li>Rs. 700</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(25)"><span id="btntext25">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer25"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>S.I. for 1 year = Rs. (854 - 815) = Rs. 39.</p><p>S.I. for 3 year = Rs.(39 x 3) = Rs. 117.</p><p>Principal = Rs. (815 - 117) = Rs. 698.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">26) Mr. Thomas contributed a measure of Rs. 13,900 separated in two different plans A and B at the simple interest loan fee of 14% p.a. and 11% p.a. respectively. If that the aggregate sum of basic premium earned in 2 years be Rs. 3508, what was the sum invested into Scheme B?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 6400</li><li>Rs. 6500</li><li>Rs. 7200</li><li>Rs. 7500</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(26)"><span id="btntext26">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer26"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Let the aggregate invested in Scheme A be Rs. x and that in Scheme B be Rs. (13900 - x).</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q26.png"/></p><p>28x - 22x = 350800 - (13900 x 22)<br/>6x = 45000<br/>x = 7500.</p><p>So, aggregate invested in Scheme B = Rs. (13900 - 7500) = Rs. 6400.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">27) A total got an aggregate basic interest of Rs. 4016.25 at the rate of 9 p.c. p.a. in 5 years. What is the total?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 4462.50</li><li>Rs. 8032.50</li><li>Rs. 8900</li><li>Rs. 8925</li><li>None of these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(27)"><span id="btntext27">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer27"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> D</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q27.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">28) How much time will it take for a measure of Rs. 450 to yield Rs. 81 as interest at 4.5% for each annum of simple interest?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>3.5 years</li><li>4 years</li><li>4.5 years</li><li>5 years</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(28)"><span id="btntext28">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer28"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q28.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">29) A man purchases a book for Rs.29.50 and offers it for Rs 31.10. Discover his gain percent.</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>8.1%</li><li>5.4%</li><li>9.8%</li><li>2.4%</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(29)"><span id="btntext29">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer29"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>So we have C.P. = 29.50</p><p>S.P. = 31.10</p><p>Gain = 31.10 - 29.50 = Rs. 1.6</p><p>Gain %=( Gain/Cost*100)%</p><p>= (1.6/29.50*100)%=5.4%</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">30) If log 2 = 0.3010 and log 3 = 0.4771, the value of log5 512 is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>2.870</li><li>2.967</li><li>3.876</li><li>3.912</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(30)"><span id="btntext30">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer30"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">31) The banker discount on a bill due 4 months subsequently at 15% is Rs. 420. The Banker discount is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 400</li><li>Rs. 360</li><li>Rs. 480</li><li>Rs. 320</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(31)"><span id="btntext31">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer31"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q31.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">32) The investor's discount on Rs. 1600 at 15% per annum is the equal as a true discount on Rs. 1680 for a similar time and at an equal rate. The time is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>3 months</li><li>4 months</li><li>7 months</li><li>8 months</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(32)"><span id="btntext32">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer32"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>S.I. on Rs. 1600 = T.D. on Rs. 1680.</p><p>Rs. 1600 is the P.W. of Rs. 1680, i.e., Rs. 80 is on Rs. 1600 at 15%.</p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q32.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">33) The banker's gain at a specific entirety due 2 years consequently at 10% per annum is Rs. 24. The present worth is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 480</li><li>Rs. 520</li><li>Rs. 600</li><li>Rs. 960</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(33)"><span id="btntext33">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer33"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q33.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">34) The banker's gain on an aggregate due 3 years consequently at 12% per annum is Rs. 270. The banker discount is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>Rs. 960</li><li>Rs. 840</li><li>Rs. 1020</li><li>Rs. 760</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(34)"><span id="btntext34">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer34"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> C</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q34.png"/></p><p>B.D. = Rs. (750 + 270) = Rs. 1020.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">35) A man crosses a 600 m long road in 5 minutes. What is his speed in km per hour?</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>3.6</li><li>7.2</li><li>8.4</li><li>10</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(35)"><span id="btntext35">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer35"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> B</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q35.png"/></p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">36) A plane covers a specific distance at a speed of 240 km ph in 5 hours. To cover a similar distance in <img alt="Microsoft Interview Questions" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/interview/images/microsoft-interview-question-apt-q36.png" style="margin:5px 4px -15px 0"/> hours, it must go at a speed of:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>300 km ph</li><li>360 km ph</li><li>600 km ph</li><li>720 km ph</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(36)"><span id="btntext36">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer36"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> D</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Distance = (240 x 5) = 1200 km.</p><p>Speed = Distance/Time</p><p>Speed = 1200/ (5/3) km/hr.</p><p>Appropriate speed = 1200 x 3/5 km/hr= 720 km/hr.</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">37) If a man strolls at 14 km/hr rather than 10 km/hr, he would have strolled 20 km more. The actual distance traveled by him is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>50 km</li><li>56 km</li><li>70 km</li><li>80 km</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(37)"><span id="btntext37">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer37"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p></div><hr/><h2 class="h4">38) A train can travel half quicker than a car. Both begin from point A in the meantime and achieve point B 75 km from A in the meantime. In transit, in any case, the train lost around 12.5 minutes while stopping at the stations. The speed of the car is:</h2><ol class="pointsu"><li>100 km ph</li><li>110 km ph</li><li>120 km ph</li><li>130 km ph</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(38)"><span id="btntext38">Show Answer</span></button><div class="testanswer" id="answer38"><p><strong>Answer:</st